<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ============================================================
    menu_bottom_nav.xml — bottom navigation items
    ===
    Consumed by:
      - activity_main.xml  (app:menu="@menu/menu_bottom_nav")
      - MainActivity.java  (R.id.nav_chats / nav_people / nav_profile)

    Three items, in this order:
      1. Chats    → primary screen, default tab, chat list
      2. People   → user search / start new conversation
      3. Profile  → own profile, settings, logout

    Constraints on this file:

    1. STABLE IDS.
       The three ids are referenced by name from MainActivity
       via R.id.nav_chats / nav_people / nav_profile. They are
       the fragment-switching keys. Renaming an id here requires
       a matching rename in MainActivity — the compiler will
       catch it, but the intent is to keep these stable for the
       life of the app.

    2. ICONS ARE 24dp MONOCHROME VECTORS.
       The three icons are created next (ic_nav_chats.xml,
       ic_nav_people.xml, ic_nav_profile.xml). They follow the
       same template-fill + view-tint pattern as every other
       icon in the project: fill is white, the BottomNavigationView
       applies the theme's tint (colorPrimary for selected,
       onSurfaceVariant for unselected) via its built-in state
       list. Do NOT set android:iconTint here — BottomNavigationView
       manages tinting internally.

    3. THREE ITEMS, NO MORE.
       Bottom navigation with >3 items becomes a "tab bar with
       labels squeezed to 10sp." Material's recommendation is
       3-5 items; with exactly 3, labels have plenty of room
       and the pattern is at its most legible. Do not add a
       fourth item ("Search" or "Settings") — search is
       accessible from the Chats screen's search field, and
       Settings is reachable from the Profile screen. Adding
       either as a nav item would be redundant and would
       crowd the bar.

    4. CHECKABLE BEHAVIOR IS IMPLICIT.
       android:checkable="true" is set on each item because
       BottomNavigationView needs a checkable item group to
       drive its "selected tab" state (the Material 3 pill
       background, the primary-color icon tint). Without it,
       the nav would render all items as "unselected" and the
       selected-state styling would not appear.

    5. NO android:iconTint OR app:itemIconTint.
       BottomNavigationView applies its own state-list tint
       based on the item's checked state and the theme's
       colorPrimary / colorOnSurfaceVariant. Adding a per-item
       tint would override that with a fixed color, breaking
       the selected/unselected visual contrast.
    ============================================================
-->
<menu xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!-- ============================================================
         CHATS — default tab, first item
         ============================================================ -->
    <item
        android:id="@+id/nav_chats"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_nav_chats"
        android:title="@string/nav_chats"
        android:checkable="true" />

    <!-- ============================================================
         PEOPLE — user search / start new conversation
         ============================================================ -->
    <item
        android:id="@+id/nav_people"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_nav_people"
        android:title="@string/nav_people"
        android:checkable="true" />

    <!-- ============================================================
         PROFILE — own profile, settings, logout
         ============================================================ -->
    <item
        android:id="@+id/nav_profile"
        android:icon="@drawable/ic_nav_profile"
        android:title="@string/nav_profile"
        android:checkable="true" />

</menu>
